# Hephaestus backend (api/hephaestus.js) — set these in the Vercel project's
# Environment Variables (Settings → Environment Variables), NOT in the repo.
# For local `vercel dev`, copy this to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill it in.

# Google AI Studio (Gemini) API key — format "AIza…". Get one at
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey . The free tier needs no billing.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional model override. Default: gemini-3.5-flash-lite.
# (gemini-2.5-flash-lite was the default until 2026-08-24, when it began
# returning 404 "no longer available to new users".) Live free-tier rate limits
# are shown in AI Studio; Google no longer publishes static per-model numbers.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# ── OpenRouter (optional, and preferred when set) ──────────────────────────
# If this is set, api/hephaestus.js routes to OpenRouter instead of Gemini and
# converts the reply back into the shape the client already parses — no client
# change, no redeploy needed to switch back (just unset it).
#
# Default model: deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash. That is a measured choice — bench/
# scored it 27/29 BLIND on this exact tool contract. Measured cost is about
# $0.000125 per turn, so a full build conversation runs roughly $0.0008.
#
# WARNING: this endpoint is public and unauthenticated. On the Gemini free tier
# abuse just produced 429s; with a paid OpenRouter key it spends real money. Per
# request is bounded (max_tokens 1024, conversation capped at 40 turns), but
# per day is not. Set a spend limit on the OpenRouter key.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
